## 88. Merge Sorted Array

## Approach
Create a new array merge of size m + n.
Use two pointers i and j for nums1 and nums2.
Compare the elements of both arrays.
Put the smaller element into merge.
If both elements are equal, put both into merge.
Move the pointer after taking an element.
When one array is finished, copy the remaining elements from the other array.
Finally, copy all elements from merge back into nums1.

## Complexity
Time: O(m + n)
Space: O(m + n) because we create the merge array.

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public void merge(int[] nums1, int m, int[] nums2, int n) {
        int[] merge = new int[n + m];
        int index = 0;
        int i = 0;
        int j = 0;
        while (i < m && j < n) {
            if (nums1[i] < nums2[j]) {
                merge[index] = nums1[i];
                index++;
                i++;
            } else if (nums1[i] > nums2[j]) {
                merge[index] = nums2[j];
                index++;
                j++;
            } else {
                merge[index++] = nums1[i];
                merge[index++] = nums2[j];
                i++;
                j++;
            }
        }

        while (i < m) {
            merge[index] = nums1[i];
            index++;
            i++;
        }

        while (j < n) {
            merge[index] = nums2[j];
            index++;
            j++;
        }

        for (int k = 0; k < (n + m); k++) {
            nums1[k] = merge[k];
        }

    }
}
